[{"_1":2},"routes/docs-slug",{"_3":4},"data",{"_5":6,"_7":8},"content","# Writing Copilot\n\nThe Writing Copilot is a context-aware AI assistant integrated directly into your workspace. It doesn't just generate text; it understands your world.\n\n## Key Features\n\n### 1. Context Scoping\nYou can control exactly what the AI \"sees\" during a session:\n- **Chapter Scope**: Focuses the AI's attention only on the current chapter. Ideal for brainstorming dialogue or describing a specific scene.\n- **Novel Scope**: Allows the AI to reference your entire Series Bible and all previous chapters. Use this for global research or cross-checking facts.\n\n### 2. Citations & References\nTransparency is key. When the AI answers a question or helps you brainstorm, it provides **Citations**.\n- Clicking a citation opens the **Reference Sidebar**.\n- You can see exactly which character profile, location, or previous chapter the AI is referencing.\n\n### 3. Context Graph\nFor Pro users, the **Context Graph** provides a visual map of the AI's \"thought process.\"\n- See which Entities and Arcs are currently \"active\" in the AI's memory.\n- Manually pin or unpin lore to fine-tune the AI's creative direction.\n\n## How to Use\n1. Open the **Chat Panel** on the right side of the editor.\n2. Select your **Scope** (Chapter or Novel) at the bottom.\n3. Ask a question or give a command (e.g., *\"Summarize the tension between Elias and the Council in Chapter 3\"*).\n4. Review the citations to ensure consistency with your vision.\n","slug","copilot"]
